From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:30:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-133: the CSV table's Name Box (Ctrl+G = go to C12
 / B2:D5 / a row) and AutoFit (a double click on a column boundary) (0.133.0)

Excel's Name Box and Go To, and AutoFit Column Width:
- media/csv.js: the Name Box at the left of the toolbar shows the active cell; Ctrl+G (or a
  click) goes into it; C12, B2:D5 (its top-left active), a row number, a column letter + Enter
  = there, the block selected; a place the table does not have = said, nothing moved; Esc =
  back. A double click on a column heading's boundary = the width of its longest value (every
  row, the table's own font, the title row in bold); with whole columns selected, each of them.
  Copy / paste in the Name Box stay its own text.
- package.json: Ctrl+G and Shift+F10 are the table's while it is active (VS Code's Go to Line
  no longer opens over it); F5 stays VS Code's (it starts a debug run).
- tests: csv_driver (Name Box, AutoFit after a drag narrower), csv_realinput (real Ctrl+G + c3,
  a real double click on the boundary), smoke (the keybindings).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
